            <ArticleTitle>[Microscopic lesions of the myocardium in acute coronary heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A statisticomathematical analysis of microscopic changes in the myocardium has established pathognomonic and differential-diagnostic morphological signs for diagnosis of acute ischemic heart disease--acute coronary failure and acute myocardial infarction at the prenecrotic stage. The results of chromotrop 2B water blue staining of histological preparations and polarization microscopy were compared.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
